  "notes": "**Repeater operation.** Aether DV now knows where your data goes on a D-STAR repeater and takes turns with voice users.\n\n- **Choose who receives your data, per radio port:** this repeater only (the default), or everyone on the reflector it's linked to. Set it in the config file's `[port.route]` section. The example configs show how.\n- **Checks the radio before sending.** UR, R1 and R2 must match the choice: R2 blank keeps data on the repeater, R2 = the gateway sends it to the reflector.\n  - On radios with CI-V (the IC-9700, and others where the radio answers), Aether DV reads them itself.\n  - Otherwise it asks you to confirm them each session, after a reconnect, and after 30 minutes without sending.\n- **Never re-sends a gateway command.** A link or unlink command left in UR is blocked when R2 is the gateway.\n- **Reflector scope is deliberate.** You confirm it once per session and again when the link changes. Files there are limited to 8 KiB, and broadcast pings aren't answered.\n- **Takes turns with voice.** Where CI-V reports the channel, Aether DV waits for voice to end plus a 10-second gap. It also:\n  - keeps each transmission short and leaves gaps between them so others can break in;\n  - keeps to an air-time budget: 25 % on a repeater, 10 % on a reflector;\n  - pauses transfer timers while someone else holds the channel.\n- **Pause sending** from the port panel, or for 30 minutes during a net.\n- **Port panel.** Click a port in the top bar to see the radio's call signs next to what's needed, and why the port is waiting. It also has a repeater access check, which reports the repeater's acknowledgement, BER and linked reflector.\n- **Radio Setup:** each radio has a new \"Using a repeater\" section.\n\nWithout CI-V, voice users are only noticed when their radio sends position data. Pause sending during voice contacts and nets.\n\nStill **tested in simulation only**: a simulated IC-9700 and a simulated repeater. Nothing has been tested through a real repeater or with real D-RATS stations yet, and the timing values will change after on-air tests.",
